Z||000000||pherder||01-24-2000||12:42 PM||||Forumees!<P>Somewhere, somehow, some person, some ... whatever, got me to order GM parts @ Lustine Online ... (Thank you whomever you were!)<P>I did and their prices were great!  The problem came Saturday by FedEX.  I ordered one of a sunroof gasket and got 10!!!! I ordered one right and left side dew wipes and got 10 right side only.  I got two right side rain drip moldings, and the list goes on!!<P>Their shopping cart program is NOT setup to take any of the "special order" items and will take the part number that preceeds it and keep the number ordered with it thus duplicating the part order.  That is why I got all the mess I got.<P>I just spoke to Dennis @ Lustine (he handles the Inet orders) and he is sending a recall for the unwanted parts.<P>He also explained why I had the mess (see above) and that their web pages are being redone to be better.  Right now, the web pages do not explain that you CAN NOT order special order parts thru the shopping cart.  That is handled thru the email at this time (you send an email asking for a quote and they get back to you in a day or two with the price and then you order by return email.)<P>I will keep the list advised on how I get credit back on the unwanted parts and if treated like I was on the phone (great, BTW), I will use them again!<P>Their URL is:   <A HREF="http://www.lustineparts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lustineparts.com/</A> <P>Paul<P>||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||01-24-2000||09:05 PM||||I've been checking out <A HREF="http://www.wrenchead.com" TARGET=_blank>Wrenchead</A> They also have many AC-Delco (Original GM) parts that are often listed as dealer only at the chain stores, and the prices are better than most dealers. They also have more complete listings for Borg Warner and others than the chains. ((Turns out that the MAT sensor for 87-88 4 cyl is available as something besides AC delco.))<P>Since I semi need a new MAT I think I may test them a bit this week. (MAT is one of the few I haven't just flat replaced yet.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||mutfish||01-24-2000||09:44 PM||||I've used Wrenchead a few times in the past month or so,I have to say I'm satisfied with their service. First part I ordered was a TPS for a 2.8,when it arrived it was in a bubble pack envelope and was crushed.I called customer service and they sent another part right then and there.They also picked up the damaged part(UPS).The new TPS was double boxed in bubble rap.Just installed a p/s pump from them for my Grand Am,was about half of what my local Pontiac dealer wanted.My usual parts outlet couldn't even get one.||||reg||1
